<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Antoine, Duke of Brabant</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1384">1384</a>–<a href="/years/1415">1415</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Anthony, Duke of Brabant · Of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-valois">House of Valois</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Antoine of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a> was duke of Brabant and Limburg from 1406 until 1415, a younger son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-the-bold">Philip the Bold</a> of Burgundy. His great-aunt Duchess Joanna made him her heir, and he governed Brabant from 1404 and recovered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antwerp">Antwerp</a> for the duchy. He was killed fighting for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-agincourt">Battle of Agincourt</a> in 1415, and his sons John IV and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-of-saint-pol">Philip of Saint-Pol</a> succeeded him in turn.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/antoine-duke-of-brabant.jpg" alt="Antoine, Duke of Brabant" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NumisAntica · CC BY-SA 3.0 nl · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hertog_van_Brabant_Limburg_Anton_van_Bourgondie_-_AR_Groot_-_1-2_Botdrager_Leuven.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Duchess Joanna, childless, passed the duchy to her great-nephew <b>Antoine of Burgundy</b>, a younger son of Philip the Bold, who was killed at the Battle of Agincourt in 1415; after his sons John IV and Philip of Saint-Pol died without heirs, Philip the Good of Burgundy inherited Brabant…</blockquote><a href="/empire/duchy-of-brabant">Duchy of Brabant · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li></ul></section>
